" 1 Overview  2 Sites  3 VLANs  4 MACs  5 Log  6 Setup  7 Breakout  8 Settings   "
"┌ Help (Esc closes, Up/Down scrolls) ──────────────────────────────────────────┐"
"│ 1 Overview                                                                   ║"
"│   Up/Down             select a peer, below them a site of the network        ║"
"│   Enter               details: traffic graph, round trips, counters          █"
"│   o                   the selected site online or offline (to the review)    █"
"│   u                   unblock the port of the peer (loop guard)              ║"
"│   U                   unblock a trunk port (loop guard)                      ║"
"│   p                   measure the path MTU to all peers now                  ║"
"│   t                   optimize the selected tunnel (RPS transport auto)      ║"
"│   z                   the graphs: the last 2 min, 10 min or 1 h              ║"
"│   Green: reachable and up. Yellow: degraded (port down or offline, config    ║"
"│   differs, late replies). Red: unreachable or blocked by the loop guard. The ║"
"│   graphs show what came in above the line (green) and what went out below it ║"
"│   (magenta), each on its own scale; the daemon records the last hour, LOAD   ║"
"│   compares the tunnels. With RPS transport auto (Settings 8), optimizing a   ║"
"│   tunnel (by itself when it comes up, or t) measures for about 30 s with the ║"
"│   peer whether spreading the receive work over the cores (RPS) helps, with   ║"
"│   full load on the transport meanwhile: a line above the peers, "tuning…" in ║"
"│   its row and the status line show it; its details (Enter) what was kept.    ║"
"│                                                                              ║"
"└──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘"
"                          1 blocked, 1 down (see 1)  draft: no changes  heim r7 "
" Up/Down  scroll   Esc  close                                                   "
